It would be interesting to see which scales lambda (as in lines 219, 220) have actually been obtained from the training. Do they differ significantly for different datasets? Would an equidistant choice of lambda be sufficient?
Similarly it would be interesting to see the relative strengths of the lambda_A/ lambda_A^{s_i} (as in eq.7). From a theoretical perspective (thinking of spectral clustering) one would assume that mostly low frequency modes are relevant for the community dataset, is that really the case?
Lastly, it would be interesting to see whether the performance increase obtained from the spectrally filtered adjacency matrix is any better than just introducing A^{s_i}

